14. Importance of Endpoint Security Monitoring

Endpoint monitoring is important because computers are frequently targeted by cyber threats.

It helps us:

- Detect malware and suspicious activities.
- Check whether antivirus protection is working.
- Identify security problems.
- Monitor firewall protection.
- Protect important files and information.
- Respond to detected threats.
- Improve the overall security of the computer.


15. Advantages of Microsoft Defender

Some of the main advantages of Microsoft Defender are:

- It is built into Windows.
- It provides real-time protection.
- It supports different types of security scans.
- It helps detect malware and other threats.
- It provides firewall and network protection.
- It keeps a record of security actions in Protection History.
- Its status can be checked using PowerShell.
- It provides useful basic protection without requiring a separate antivirus program.



16. Limitations

Microsoft Defender provides useful protection, but no antivirus solution can guarantee complete protection from every cyberattack.

The user should also keep Windows updated, avoid suspicious files and links, use strong passwords, and follow safe cybersecurity practices.


